- Confirmed SYSPROP evidence:
  - Register 16: System Properties (SYSPROP), offset 0x14C, page 299.
  - Dynamic Power Management states that SYSPROP indicates whether low-power features are supported on a given MCU.
  - Relevant documented SYSPROP fields are FPU, LDOSEQ, FLASHLPM, SRAMLPM, SRAMSM, PIOSCPDE, TSPDE, and LDOSME.
- Confirmed FLASHPP and SSIZE evidence:
  - Register 11: Flash Peripheral Properties (FLASHPP), offset 0xFC0, page 675.
  - Register 12: SRAM Size (SSIZE), offset 0xFC4, page 677.
  - Both registers appear under Chapter 8 Internal Memory at base 0x400F.D000, not in the SYSCTL register block.
  - FLASHPP fields relevant to capability discovery are PFC, FMM, DFA, EESS, MAINSS, and SIZE.
  - SSIZE provides a single implemented SRAM size field, SIZE.
- Capability-model conclusion from the manual:
  - Section 5.2.1 says TM4C129 capability information comes from DID0/DID1, SYSCTL Peripheral Present registers at offset 0x300, and per-peripheral Properties registers at offset 0xFC0.
  - This supports using SYSPROP plus FLASHPP and SSIZE as current documented capability targets instead of treating legacy DC0/DC1 names as authoritative TM4C129 SYSCTL registers.
- Surrounding implementation review:
  - Existing repo register defines include a SYSPROP raw header, which is consistent with the manual-backed SYSCTL register.
  - Earlier workspace manual audits already established that DC0/DC1 do not appear in the TM4C129 SYSCTL register map.
